!! Vitals

* ''Branch'' `feature/lararium-node-5`, ahead of `origin` — `git rev-list --count origin/feature/lararium-node-5..HEAD` reads the unpushed commits; the operator pushes. Crew-held dirt in the tree: `mempalace` (submodule), `tests/harness/instance.ts`, untracked `tests/e2e/nexus-offering-replication.test.ts` and `packages/lararium-node/tests/origin-standing.test.ts`, `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/`, `.worktrees/`, `.claude/worktrees/`. Never commit, stash, or revert those.
* ''Corpus'': every tracked `bags/*.mem` reads canonical under `lares meme check`; `tools/bcc-witness.sh` reads every block check `ok`.
* ''The witness fleet'' (`tools/witness-all.sh`, what CI runs) ends on a verdict table, one line per witness with its own exit code — count the reds there, never in the transcript. Two of 32 read red after a fresh build: `vessel-parity-witness` (`makePersonaGroupIdentityRing` composes on node only — the browser side is owed) and `round-trip-witness` (`lararium-tw5` `tests/grammar-in-a-wiki.test.ts` runs past the default 5 s under load; it passes alone at a 60 s timeout). Every other witness reads ok, `contract-witness` among them (on the fold, `#/wounds` P1); `symbol-anchor-witness` holds at its ceiling of 34; `unbuilt-laws-witness` reads 12 declared, 12 still red. Each dist-reading witness refuses a stale build by name (exit 2) — rebuild the named package, run `node tools/stamp-build.mjs . --pkg <name>`, re-run; a comment edit in a package's `src/` stales its dist too.
* ''Typecheck'' (`tools/typecheck-witness.sh`): every package clean across 11 projects.
* ''CI'' (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): the last run read a pushed head behind the local tree — `gh run list --branch feature/lararium-node-5` names it. Its reds and what answers each in the unpushed commits: Typecheck (`OraclePointer.version`, answered by the oracle panel's act CID), Grammar artifact gates (the wasm built after the TS host read it, answered by the build order), the Sensorium suite (the meme-tools fixture's socket path, answered by pytest's tmp; `test_structure_router` stays red — `#/wounds` P1), Witnesses (`typecheck`, `unbuilt-laws` reading an escape-coloured summary — answered — and `vessel-parity`, which stands), and E2E (runs out its ceiling — `#/wounds` P1). Build + generated freshness, Pristine upstream and Boot budget read green. `.github/workflows/held-out.yml` failed validation at 0s on that push; the unpushed tree resolves its evidence path inside the run step. The next push is the witness for the answers.
* ''The tree is shared'': a parallel lane edits `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/wsl2/**` and `tools/wsl2/**` and re-stamps after editing — a witness run mid-edit reads its carriers as drifted for a minute. Re-run before believing a red there.
* ''Known test reds'' and their owners:
** `lararium-node` `tests/bind-under-handle.test.ts` — crew: the joinee boot path never supplies `expectedEpoch` (the binding gate needs the live lease epoch, as `face-join.ts` supplies it); never revert the gate.
** `lares-cli` `tests/help-door-meme.test.ts`, `tests/nexus-verb-reach.test.ts` — crew: `nexus offering` keeps its help text outside the command registry.
** `lararium-sensorium` `scripts/test_structure_router.py::test_ahu_block_nests_inner_sigils` — `#/wounds` P1.
** `lararium-tw5` `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts` (Chromium legs) and `tests/meme-routes.e2e.test.ts` — environmental (browser / server sockets).
** `lararium-tw5` corpus suites can fail on `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/wsl2/*.mem` while that lane edits them — its owner's to settle.
** `lararium-tw5` `tests/grammar-in-a-wiki.test.ts` — a corpus-wide walk that times out at the default 5 s under load; passes alone.
** Every staged e2e suite but the two herm suites — `#/wounds` P1.

