<<~ ahu #/cold-start>>

!! Cold start

# `export LAR_BAGS=/tmp/lar-scratch-<you>` before any `lares` command or in-tree boot — a bare in-tree boot writes projection artifacts into the tracked tree.
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, then `pnpm -r build`, then `pnpm --filter @lararium/tw5 build:tw5-vendor` (the TW5 core blob `head-parity` and `scripts/smoke-plugin-boot.ts` need — `pnpm -r build` does not produce it), then `node tools/stamp-build.mjs`.
# A fresh `git worktree` holds empty submodules (`TiddlyWiki5`, `VSCode-TW5-Syntax`, `mempalace`); populate them before building there.
# `lares-cli` `tests/pour-repave.test.ts` needs the dev-root marker (`LAR_DEV_REPO_ROOT=1` or the gitignored `lar-dev-root.json`).
# The tw5 plugin bundle (`packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/lares-memetic-wikitext.json`, `plugins/standalone/*`, `src/plugin-tiddler.generated.ts`) is tracked and must equal a fresh build — rebuild after any tw5 source or tiddler change and commit it with the change. CI's `build-freshness` job checks it once CI runs.
# Run `bash tools/witness-all.sh` for the whole fleet — a hand-picked subset of witnesses reads greener than the tree.
# Read `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot` (the boot seed), then this carrier, then the rulings memory (`project_grammar_as_tiddlers_rulings.md`) before touching grammar, frame, or ingest code.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/wounds>>

!! Open wounds, by priority

''P1 — owed now''
* ''E2E reds on every staged vessel.'' The explicit-origin law (`1c502ba92`) refuses a vessel booted under a scratch `LAR_ROOT`, which reads its own absent `config.json`: boot composes the Web and oracle origins for every face and refuses with "Web origin must be declared". The herm suites declare `LAR_SAME_ORIGIN=true` for themselves (`tests/e2e/herm-floor.test.ts`, `tests/e2e/herm-reshares-public-blob.e2e.test.ts`); every other staged suite refuses. The cure waits on the operator's herm decision #3, a standing-aware origin composition. Behind it stands the lease-frontier red: "Binding Gate: current lease frontier unavailable" (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/boot-daemon-keyhive.ts:137`). CI's e2e job runs out its ceiling on these.
* ''The presented-admit gate: the cut-over (solo, open ground) and the contract-witness proof.'' What stands: `verifyPresentedAdmit` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/carriage-registry.ts`) reads a presented admit and its lineage against the deny-only board and the kapae antigen; the wire carries `presentedAdmit` and `packages/lararium-node/src/daemon-auth-gate.ts` keeps it per socket, deciding nothing; the subject stamp signs with a per-Nexus leaf (`packages/lararium-node/src/nexus-leaf.ts`); a vessel carries a SET of Nexuses (`packages/lararium-node/src/carried-set.ts`, `lares nexus seal import --carry`); the federation gate federates every carried island's boards. ''The cut-over'' moves the daemon's carriage decision off the folded members board (`foldCarriageSet` → `nexus-carriage.ts`) onto the verifier, and fills the boot seat that reads no contract nym (`open-node-vessel.ts`, `contractNymAtThisSeat`). The docblocks at `nexus-carriage.ts:36`, `:271` and `nexus-refresh.ts:61` name the fold "this vessel's own board" and move with it. Its globs stand on no hearth's ground; it lands under commit isolation. ''The proof'': `tools/contract-witness.sh` reads green today on the fold; it takes five checks over the presented admit and an e2e. Canon: `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu` `#/nexus-scale`.
* ''The quoteblock floor in live use.'' `packages/lararium-tw5/src/modules/meme-backstop.ts` `runChildGate` fences a child body whose splice breaks the composed root, only on a bag this hearth keeps, and raises `quoteblocked`; a peer's child on a bag this hearth does not keep surfaces only. Unit-tested; unexercised against real concurrent browser saves — watch it, and add a test for any shape it mis-attributes.
* ''Parallel drafts reach no wiki.'' `packages/lararium-mesh/src/parallel-drafts.ts` answers one attributed TW5 draft per writing actor from a record's conflict ops, and `AutomergeDocStore` raises the surface; no wiki shows them. Whether a losing draft persists durably is the operator's ruling (P2).
* ''A Sensorium red.'' `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/test_structure_router.py::test_ahu_block_nests_inner_sigils` reads one inner sigil where it asserts two — red on the desk and in CI.

''P2 — needs the operator''
* ''The herm's Web surface, decisions 1–5'' — #3, the standing-aware origin composition, gates the e2e red above.
* ''Parallel drafts: does a loser persist durably?''
* ''Grammar submissions'': whether the Nexus Kahu or the corpus-kahu receive them.
* ''The offering's `offer`/`witness` caps'' against the Lamplighter stack.
* ''Engine cadence, still open'' (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu` `#/contract`): who holds a cadence share; one daemon hosting two engine epochs; whether partial conformance lands before `kahuli engine` un-holds.
* ''Backstop seam (b), PHASE 5'' (`tests/meme-backstop.test.ts`): two child-edit cases the test marks as the operator's call.
* ''Ruling-gated mesh modules'' (listed in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/index.ts`'s header): `recipe`, `readiness`, `reaction-graph` (canon memes pin their mesh `source-file`), `pronaos`, `offering-inspection` (own mesh-namespace memes). Each moves or stays only by ruling.
* ''The capture cell'' sits isolated for review in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-node/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/capture/`, `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/capture/`. Canon (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/capture-annotation-model`, the sensorium-machina S5 ruling) places capture in Python per stream with the TS @daemon coordinating only; the TS cell carries the live path. Rule: retire it to Python, or re-home it.
* ''The wild-bytes line'' — tolerate bytes the house cannot re-make (history, outside bytes), cut tolerance for state it can re-found — awaits canonizing beside the no-legacy law. `packages/lararium-mesh/src/capture/turn-harvest.ts` keeps its retired-head tolerance for old transcripts under it.
* ''`bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/handoff.mem` `#/shift-2026-09-13-meme-hearth`'' (~:516) carries a suspended loop `@_:operator-rebooted-before-steering` (the watcher talk-story) — reconvene or release.
* ''The tree's git config'': restore `core.bare = false` (operator's hand only).

''Research owed''
* ''Whole-chunk grain of the quoteblock floor'' (a carrier arriving whole and partially un-decomposable → fence the whole chunk at the ingest seat), specified in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/ahu#/quoteblock-floor`, unbuilt. The spec names WHAT fences and not WHERE: which ingest door(s) seat it, how "partially un-decomposable" decides before any family stands, and how it composes with a torn frame's refusal.

''P3 — deferred by law or by the operator''
* ''The Sensorium's logic'' (`packages/lararium-sensorium/**`, tw5 `form-layer/**`, mesh `ffz-project`, `clock-recovery`, coupling/metric modules): the measure-servo aliases in `ffz-project.ts`, one five-band ladder (Title case `ApertureBand`, the others derived), the `lar_feedback` output field name. Frames inside it stay in scope for healing at any time.
* ''Tangle, the putback law, the tongue fold'' — gated on a real return trip and a whole regeneration of `packages/tree-sitter-memetic-wikitext` (mirror pairing, round-trip CI, Markdown injection into `hana`). The aka/weave rhyme (`memetic-wikitext-framing.mem` Annex) waits on tangle.
* ''A relay-stream profile'' — carriers close on EOT in flight; SYN (`&#x0016;`) stays the one reserved stream mark; the profile defines batch framing and resynchronisation.
* ''A carrier seal'' — re-mint an attestation mark with a computed, verified check when signing lands.
* ''EOT targeting'' — what a resolved `-> to=` would name (the declared-unresolved meaning stands).
* ''A standing whole-tree gate'' (build every package from clean, run every witness and suite) — run as a spirit pass, not built into the CLI or a trigger.

